   $q$A painter covers $\frac{3}{8}$ of a wall in $\frac{1}{6}$ of an hour at a constant rate. Which equation gives the part of a wall $y$ painted in $x$ hours?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$y = \\frac{1}{16}x$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"multiplied-instead-of-divided"},{"text":"$y = \\frac{4}{9}x$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"divided-time-by-amount"},{"text":"$y = \\frac{9}{4}x$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$y = \\frac{3}{8}x$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-amount-as-rate"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$y = \frac{9}{4}x$$q$, $q$The constant of proportionality is walls per hour: $\frac{3}{8} \div \frac{1}{6} = \frac{3}{8} \times 6 = \frac{18}{8} = \frac{9}{4}$, so $y = \frac{9}{4}x$. The choice $y = \frac{1}{16}x$ multiplies $\frac{3}{8}$ by $\frac{1}{6}$ instead of dividing.$q$, 'draft', null)
